Subject: [PATCH] One libretro button per N64 button, no C-button options

The independent C-button mapping, always: C-Up, C-Down, ... each a
RetroPad button, no shift layer on R2. corehost lists the descriptors as
rows, in their order, and the player binds a combo to each, so every row
has to be a real N64 input, listed as the pad has them: stick, A, B, Z,
Start, L, R, C buttons, D-pad. The C buttons are not also described on
the right stick, and the options that only serve the RetroPad layout
(which button is which C button, the mapping switch, the stick deadzone)
are gone. The deadzone is 0 without its option, right for a stick that is
buttons.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [corehost policy]
---
diff -ru a/custom/mupen64plus-core/plugin/emulate_game_controller_via_libretro.c b/custom/mupen64plus-core/plugin/emulate_game_controller_via_libretro.c
